---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Why does your portfolio look plain?">
  <h1 class="title">why does your portfolio look like this?</h1>
  <div class="stack">
    <div>
      <h2 class="heading">intentional</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        the design strips everything back to what matters: structure,
        hierarchy, content. no gradients to hide weak ideas, no carousels to
        distract from bad work. one column, one typeface, and the actual work.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="heading">builder first</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        i'm a builder. the most important thing on this site is what i'm
        building right now, and what i've built. if something doesn't help you
        understand who i am or what i build, it doesn't belong here.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2 class="heading">copycats</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        inspiration drives creativity. i've refined my skills by learning from
        the work of others, and i welcome anyone who finds value in what i
        create. there's a clear line between drawing inspiration and outright
        copying. blatantly replicating and claiming someone else's work as your
        own is unacceptable.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
